    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12075" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">custōdītĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		custodio. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.,
				<i>guardianship, care</i>: custoditio est opera ad
			custodiendum quid sumpta, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest.
				p. 61, 15</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a keeping,
				observance</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Sap. 6, 19</span></i>
			.</div>
